=1 1 23
+    The DZ serial driver of the DECstation has the input and output
+    services of the DZ port driver in place of the interrupt service
+    routines of the 8250.
=1 23 12
+VOID
+SerialInputService(
+    IN PVOID ClientContext,
+    IN UCHAR InputByte,
+    IN ULONG InputStatus
=1 39 6
+    This is the input service of the port, which the DZ port driver calls
+    with each character that the line of the port receives, at the level
+    of the interrupt of the port.  It does what the interrupt service
+    routine of the 8250 does for a receive line status interrupt and a
+    received data available interrupt: the character and its receive
+    status are put where SerialReadReceiveBuffer and SerialReadLineStatus
+    read them, as the 8250 holds them in its receive buffer and line
+    status registers.
=1 51 3
+    ClientContext - This is really a pointer to the device extension for
+    this device.
+
+    InputByte - The character.
+
+    InputStatus - The receive errors of the character (dzport.h).
=1 1053 9
+    PSERIAL_DEVICE_EXTENSION Extension = ClientContext;
+    UCHAR ReceivedChar;
+
+    if (!Extension->DeviceIsOpened) {
+
+        //
+        // The port is closed: what it receives is dropped.
=1 1082 6 -4
