=1 1407 5
+BOOLEAN
+SerialOutputService(
+    IN PVOID ClientContext
=1 39 6
+    This is the output service of the port, which the DZ port driver
+    calls each time the transmitter of the line of the port is ready, at
+    the level of the interrupt of the port.  It does what the interrupt
+    service routine of the 8250 does for a transmit holding register empty
+    interrupt: unless transmission is held up, it sends the next xon, xoff,
+    immediate or write character with the output routine of the port.
=1 51 3
+    ClientContext - This is really a pointer to the device extension for
+    this device.
=1 59 3
+    TRUE if a character was sent, FALSE if the line has nothing to send
+    (the port driver then disables the transmitter of the line).
